prompt: >
  Continue in E:\Source\Rust\SLMComposer.com as the active Rust workspace for TinyRustLM, with E:\Source\Rust\MiniModel.org as the MiniModel.org site workspace. The site-folder split, source-control cleanup, MiniModel intake processing, Hugging Face option routing, roadmap, metadata-only MiniModel catalog endpoint, TinyRustLM catalog-to-local-file import slice, Chat/Advanced Tools dashboard redesign, real Model Setup sidebar, local Hugging Face conversion-script handoff, one-command Hugging Face `convert-huggingface-request` flow, sharded Hugging Face `.safetensors` source-directory conversion, self-locating `.tinyrustlm-convert.ps1` scripts, self-locating `.minimodel-peer-import.ps1` scripts, Rust `.minimodel-peer-offer` proof commands, the first MiniModel local Rust verifier (`minimodel-core` plus `minimodel` CLI), local peer-piece export/reassembly, direct known-peer HTTP `fetch-peer-pieces`, TinyRustLM.com root app route, Hugging Face/P2P enterprise quality refactor, TinyRustLM `P2P Import` peer-import request/script handoff, MiniModel `add-peer-source`, MiniModel `write-peer-source-announcement`/`apply-peer-source-announcements`, MiniModel `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcements` batch publication, MiniModel `write-peer-source-announcement-feed` plus `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcement-feed`, TinyRustLM local peer-source announcement overlay, and TinyRustLM same-origin SHA-256-bound catalog announcement feed routes are complete in local source. TinyRustLM.com and documentation sites should be deployed from source only after docs are updated and live proof is run. Start the next work by deciding the smallest peer-discovery or peer-offer publication slice that can make consenting peer endpoints discoverable without adding project-server model bytes. Keep TinyRustLM browser-local and keep project servers metadata-only: no server-side user model execution and no project-server user model bytes.
primary_goal: >
  Move from local peer-piece export/reassembly into the first consent-based peer-transfer network design slice while preserving the verifier as the authority: peers may provide chunks later, but local Rust verification and receipts remain mandatory before TinyRustLM import.
