roadmap_guardrails:
  - Rust-first P2P model exchange architecture; evaluate Pear/Bare/Hyper as tradeoffs, not core SLMComposer dependencies.
  - Source options are user-owned local files/lists, user-triggered Hugging Face discovery, and future MiniModel P2P transfer; all converge on local `.slm` verification.
  - SLMComposer Chat mode should keep Local Files, Hugging Face, P2P Exchange, prompt, and Generate visible on first load while Advanced Tools exposes diagnostics and lower-level controls.
  - SLMComposer dashboard source should remain simple on first load: left navigation, local privacy proof, model-ready toolbar, starter cards, central composer, and contained Advanced Options for pro controls.
  - Hugging Face rows are model-card metadata only; simple rows use a list-level P2P toggle, show `P2P Import` only for peer-proof MiniModel matches while P2P is enabled, show `Start Conversion` otherwise, show one disabled-P2P warning, and keep Search Metadata from closing the source chooser.
  - `P2P Import` currently saves a local `minimodel.peer_import_request.v0` JSON plus self-locating `.minimodel-peer-import.ps1` Rust reverify script; the script resolves `MINIMODEL_WORKSPACE`, keeps request/manifest/output paths beside the downloaded script, takes a consenting direct `http://` peer URL, then runs one MiniModel receiver command, `import-peer-request <request-json> <manifest> <output-dir>`, which fetches, assembles, verifies, and writes the import receipt.
  - `Start Conversion` currently saves a `minimodel.huggingface_conversion_request.v0` JSON plus self-locating `.tinyrustlm-convert.ps1`; the script resolves workspaces/source inputs from environment variables, nearby paths, a reviewed `.safetensors` beside the script, or a reviewed directory containing every listed `.safetensors` shard, then runs one TinyRustLM packer command, `convert-huggingface-request <request.json> <input.safetensors-or-directory> <output-dir> [source-shape] [quantization]`, before MiniModel `prepare-peer-share`, optional `add-peer-source` for a local with-peer entry, optional `write-peer-source-announcement` for catalog-maintainer publication, maintainer-side `apply-peer-source-announcements`, batch `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcements`, and metadata-only `write-catalog-snapshot`.
  - TinyRustLM can apply a local `minimodel.peer_source_announcement` JSON to a loaded proof-ready `models.v0.json` snapshot, validate it against the catalog entry, and re-render matching rows from `Set Peer URL` to `P2P Import`; this is still metadata-only and `import-peer-request` remains the byte path.
  - TinyRustLM can also follow catalog-declared `peer_source_announcement_route(s)` only when routes stay same-origin with the catalog and the fetched feed body matches the declared SHA-256; failed optional feeds must not create peer sources.
  - MiniModel can publish peer-source announcement feeds with `write-peer-source-announcement-feed` and route-bind them into metadata-only catalog snapshots with `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcement-feed`; the feed is JSON metadata only and must not contain model bytes or project-hosted artifact URLs.
  - 2026-07-02 intake reports are preserved under `docs/report-intake/2026-07-02/` with synthesis `tinyrustlm-minimodel-intake-synthesis-2026-07-02.md`; keep broad P2P discovery/Iroh/relays as roadmap and current direct known-peer Rust handoffs as the only implemented byte path.
  - 2026-07-02 follow-up reports are preserved under `docs/report-intake/2026-07-02-followup/` with synthesis `tinyrustlm-followup-intake-synthesis-2026-07-02.md`; keep their guidance tied to honest Hugging Face metadata, local Rust conversion, progressive disclosure, and metadata-only P2P availability.
  - Keep TinyRustLM.com `/` as the canonical public app route; `/app/` can remain a secondary route, but docs and deploy proof should target root.
  - Keep the Hugging Face UI row state centralized through shared helpers; do not reintroduce divergent simple/advanced compatibility text or per-row simple conversion controls.
  - Keep the left sidebar as real Model Setup routing only: Local .slm, Hugging Face, P2P import, Advanced tools, and documentation links. Do not reintroduce placeholder Library/Tune/Theme/settings-style controls unless they are backed by implemented behavior and tests.
  - Legal/liability boundaries must keep MiniModel.org as metadata/catalog guidance until legal review; no claims that third-party models are safe, legal, or endorsed.
  - Secure manifests must be checksum-bound and route source identity, model cards, license, tokenizer/config, eval/admission evidence, chunk/Merkle data, and signatures.
  - Tiny-model creation/import stays tied to TinyRustLM local review, conversion, validation, runtime-smoke, eval, admission, and local import receipts.
  - Project servers never run user model bytes and never serve user model bytes.
next_implementation_slice:
  - Preserve the implemented `key=value` manifest parser, duplicate-key rejection, project-server model-byte URL rejection, and server-execution rejection as the non-negotiable trust gate.
  - Design the smallest peer-discovery or peer-offer publication prototype around existing `.minimodel-peer-offer` chunk proofs, `minimodel.peer_import_request.v0` handoff files, manifest v0 chunk/Merkle fields, `minimodel.peer_piece_set.v0`, direct known-peer `fetch-peer-pieces`, `assemble-peer-pieces`, and `minimodel verify-artifact` revalidation.
  - Preserve `add-peer-source` as the direct local peer URL upgrade and `write-peer-source-announcement` plus `apply-peer-source-announcements` as the maintainer-safe portable publication flow.
  - Preserve `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcements` as the maintainer-safe batch publication flow for many entries and peer-source announcements.
  - Preserve `write-peer-source-announcement-feed` plus `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcement-feed` as the maintainer-safe route for same-origin checksum-bound availability feeds without rewriting catalog entries or hosting bytes.
  - Mirror the TinyRustLM catalog-import proof: catalog metadata can name expectations, but local verifier artifacts must come from user-supplied local paths or consent-based peer chunks reassembled locally.
  - Preserve the Hugging Face boundary: metadata discovery is allowed, project-server byte proxying and remote inference execution are not.
  - Keep any peer-transfer receipt path on `user-selected-tinyrustlm-local-file-open` after local verification passes.
  - Keep DHTs, relays, and desktop UI optional until the direct manifest/peer-offer/local-reverify path is stable.
success_criteria:
  - Active intake buckets remain empty or placeholder-only.
  - SLMComposer.com remains browser-local and user-selected local `.slm` import remains the model byte boundary.
  - MiniModel.org local schema parsing, verifier checks, peer-piece export/reassembly, and receipt writing remain stable; metadata-only catalog is current and live peer networking remains the next later phase.
  - MiniModel local verifier tests and CLI smokes remain green before any peer-transfer behavior is trusted.
  - Long-term memory remains pointer-based and checksum-bearing.
  - Before claiming completion, run relevant pointer audits and `git diff --check`.
